ReSDMAC firmware update and test utilities

This is a candidate build. Hardware validation has not been performed.
See BuildInfo for firmware commit and tool release versions.

Use the tools from your AmigaOS shell. This is not a complete Workbench disk.
If your ROM cannot boot this disk, open it from your normal AmigaOS system.

After booting this disk, resdmac, devtest and sdmac can all be run by name.
All three executables are in C:. The SDMAC test tool's command is sdmac.
Startup adds SYS:C to the command path and selects SYS: as the current directory,
where the firmware images and their CRC sidecars are stored.
If you change directories later, use SYS:10M04_update.rpd (or SYS:10M16_update.rpd).
When using the disk from an already booted system, SYS: is your system disk:
use DF0:C/resdmac -w DF0:10M04_update.rpd instead (adjust drive and FPGA model).

Firmware update (10M04 and 10M16 only):
  resdmac -w 10M04_update.rpd
  resdmac -c 10M04_update.rpd
Use 10M16_update.rpd for a 10M16 FPGA. Check your FPGA variant first.
Keep each .crc32 sidecar with its image. Verify before rebooting.
10M02 requires external programming; its POF is a separate workflow artifact.

Read Docs/updater.ReadMe, Docs/sdmac.ReadMe and Docs/devtest.ReadMe.
Run sdmac while disk activity is idle. No tools run automatically.

SDMAC and WD SCSI register checks (wait for disk activity to stop first):
  sdmac

Device probe:
  devtest -p scsi.device
Read benchmark (replace 0 with your SCSI unit):
  devtest scsi.device 0 -b
Repeated read comparison:
  devtest scsi.device 0 -i 512 -l 100

devtest -d enables writes and may destroy data. Use disposable media for
write testing, and read the upstream instructions before choosing options.
Licences for all three tools are included in Docs.
